{"id": "DfM9-VoI0_o", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why do we sing “Karpur Gauram” after every aarti? Because it describes Shiva exactly as he sits here. 🙏\n\nकर्पूरगौरं करुणावतारं\nसंसारसारं भुजगेन्द्रहारम्\n\n(Karpur gauram karunavataram, sansara saram bhujagendra haram: white as camphor, compassion in a body, the essence of this world, wearing the king of serpents as his garland.)\n\nNot blue, as most pictures show him, but white as camphor, smeared with ash. Only his throat is blue: the Halahala poison from the churning of the ocean, which he drank and held there to save the world. That is why he is Neelkanth. The Ganga rests in his matted locks, the crescent moon sits in them, and Vasuki coils round his neck.\n\nSave this for your Monday prayer, and send it to someone who sings this every evening.\n\nStories of Shiva and the gods, written for kids: Rishi Katha books at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\nFollow @therishikatha for more.\n\n#shiva #mahadev #omnamahshivaya #harharmahadev #karpurgauram neelkanth bholenath kailash shivshankar mahakal sanatandharma bhakti hindu devotional rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793544077, "like_count": 199, "comment_count": 1, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1651752390067647a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 68.749, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPtG0F4M_vCnpoqVs3gerdx3f8T2TacpBBu7wN-XszYm3DMgX_mbC0TKiFZ1duXhlnVdsqVa5MGy3IXHbJVD5zO11w93H6HHSpM6sI.mp4?_nc_cat=110&_nc_oc=AdpvBer0PWZce4udNL_Fcer5Lgy5lNtelNqwVS3edJ-h3TBSGPQ5DEZzbFfWkTG7-U31MUQC7Ym0AvTePUkf_dAx&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=1jOu6AW_inYQ7kNvwGLtKth&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=KlrNJS6EbqS_xJT1TrcqYQ&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQT